<context>
Epic EP-001 — Calendar clones through Calendar.app.
Goal: every calendar the Operator owns shows the busy slots of the other calendars, so colleagues on any account
see the real availability and the Operator gets notified on every client.
Architecture: a single Swift executable (`calsyn-cli`, Swift Package `calsyn`) talks to the calendar store
through EventKit and never touches credentials. The `reconciler` is pure logic over the `calendar-store`
abstraction, so it is tested against an in-memory fake.

Scope of this workflow:
- TASK-004: recurring, all-day, declined, free and tentative source events are cloned too, recurring occurrences
  as standalone events. Components: reconciler, calendar-store.
- TASK-009: canceled source events are never cloned, and the clones they already have are deleted at the next
  reconcile. Components: reconciler, calendar-store.
</context>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-004.md</input>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-009.md</input>
<coding_test>
- `swift test`: reconciler with recurring, all-day, declined, free, tentative fixtures (AS-09, AS-10); run on every change.
- `swift test`: fake store with a canceled source event (TASK-009, both DoD items); run on every change.
- Manual E2E: real recurring event on Exchange, `calsyn once`, check Calendar.app (AS-09); before closing TASK-004.
- Manual E2E: an Exchange meeting canceled by its organizer, run `calsyn once`, check the destination in Calendar.app; before closing TASK-009.
</coding_test>
<available_agents>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:developer" id="developer">Implements the code of the tasks and applies the fixes requested by the reviewer.</agent>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:devils-advocate" id="devils-advocate">Reviews the implementation against the tasks' Definition of Done and the epic's architecture, and reports the gaps to the developer.</agent>
</available_agents>
<tasks>
    <task id="task-004">
        `developer` implements TASK-004. Definition of Done:
        - A recurring source event → the destination shows one standalone, non-recurring clone per occurrence inside the window
        - All-day, declined, free and tentative source events are cloned
        - The clone of an all-day event is an all-day event
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="task-009">
        `developer` implements TASK-009. Definition of Done:
        - A source event whose status is canceled → after `calsyn once` no destination has a clone of it
        - A source event canceled after it was cloned → after the next reconcile its clone is gone from every destination
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="close-specs">
